1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,132
Mikoy, your dad Mario is missing?

2
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:50,759
He's looking for Chiara on his own.

3
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:52,135
I have a hunch.

4
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:54,971
He may have seen something
or followed someone.

5
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:59,184
<i>You're the reason why I lost my family.</i>

6
00:01:00,852 --> 00:01:02,479
<i>Sean has been talking</i>
<i>to someone suspicious.</i>

7
00:01:02,562 --> 00:01:05,482
There's a new character
in Chiara and Mikoy's lives.

8
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:08,068
We need to investigate this Vicky.

9
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:10,779
I can't bear to see you die.

10
00:01:10,862 --> 00:01:12,781
You and Aunt Tess have been good to me,

11
00:01:12,864 --> 00:01:14,741
so I'm here to help you.

12
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:16,159
Mario.

13
00:01:16,242 --> 00:01:17,619
The car keys.

14
00:01:17,702 --> 00:01:19,079
I need to take Chiara with me.

15
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:20,747
That's what I won't allow.

16
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:23,583
Mario, leave now before I change my mind.

17
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:37,222
<i>My prayers have been answered.</i>

18
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:44,562
Dad Mario, I'm here.

19
00:01:45,313 --> 00:01:48,233
Dad Mario. I'm so sorry.

20
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:51,319
I didn't mean to. I didn't mean to.

21
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:07,293
Dad.

22
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:09,754
Dad.

23
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:25,270
Mom, here.

24
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:31,401
Oh, honey, he doesn't like that one.

25
00:02:32,026 --> 00:02:33,611
He says it makes him look fat.

26
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:38,324
How about this one?

27
00:02:41,619 --> 00:02:43,329
He doesn't like that one either.

28
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:47,750
Because of his fair complexion,
he says it makes him look like a radish.

29
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:51,713
This one.

30
00:02:52,714 --> 00:02:53,756
This one.

31
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,258
He likes this one.

32
00:02:55,341 --> 00:02:56,426
Because, look.

33
00:02:56,509 --> 00:02:59,512
It's completely worn out
because he uses it all the time.

34
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:00,722
Because…

35
00:03:06,185 --> 00:03:09,063
This is your father's favorite.

36
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:35,632
I know that all of us here

37
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:37,800
are completely heartbroken.

38
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:43,223
There are so many questions.

39
00:03:44,641 --> 00:03:45,975
So many of us want to cry.

40
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:51,814
But you all know Dad.

41
00:03:56,694 --> 00:03:59,322
<i>Every major event in our lives…</i>

42
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:03,326
<i>is a reason to celebrate.</i>

43
00:04:03,826 --> 00:04:04,702
<i>You know, my child,</i>

44
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:07,664
<i>I never wanted you to bear this burden.</i>

45
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:09,999
<i>If only I could turn back time,</i>

46
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:13,127
<i>I wouldn't let this happen.</i>

47
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:15,088
<i>So from now on,</i>

48
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:17,966
<i>I'm here.</i>

49
00:04:19,217 --> 00:04:21,052
<i>You, Angelito, and your mother,</i>

50
00:04:22,387 --> 00:04:23,930
<i>that's what makes me so proud of you.</i>

51
00:04:25,056 --> 00:04:26,975
I want to think that's because of

52
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:29,102
how well we raised you.

53
00:04:29,894 --> 00:04:32,063
Well, of course, Dad.

54
00:04:32,146 --> 00:04:34,357
If it weren't for your and Mom's guidance,

55
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:38,319
I probably would've been picked up
from who knows where.

56
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:41,531
Maybe.

57
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:48,079
And this event is no different.

58
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:01,050
And let's never ever forget

59
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:04,679
the space he holds in our hearts.

60
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:30,288
Mario.

61
00:05:34,625 --> 00:05:36,419
Noodles for a long life.

62
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:40,423
But I don't think I believe

63
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:42,800
in that saying anymore.

64
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,973
<i>Mario, that's so unfair.</i>

65
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:52,935
<i>You left us too soon.</i>

66
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:01,110
To the best barangay captain we ever had.

67
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:05,281
And to the fair-skinned womanizer
from Albay and Cebu.

68
00:06:07,742 --> 00:06:08,785
Mario.

69
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:19,670
To our idol, whom we all look up to.

70
00:06:21,422 --> 00:06:24,592
<i>The guide who serves as a light</i>
<i>for the drunkards.</i>

71
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:26,969
<i>And for those who are down in the dumps.</i>

72
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:38,606
To my second father.

73
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:41,651
A father who, even though
we weren't related by blood,

74
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:43,319
<i>never abandoned me.</i>

75
00:06:44,112 --> 00:06:47,323
<i>A father who became more of a father</i>
<i>to me than my own father.</i>

76
00:06:47,406 --> 00:06:49,408
Cheers to Mario.

77
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:00,628
I'll miss all your jokes, Dad.

78
00:07:02,004 --> 00:07:04,799
No one should know,
not even your own mother.

79
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:06,843
You mean,

80
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:09,262
- I'd be lying to my mom.
- You wouldn't be lying.

81
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:11,556
There's just something
you didn't tell her.

82
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:15,059
<i>I'll miss how you always</i>
<i>found a way whenever</i>

83
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:16,727
life got too heavy.

84
00:07:18,938 --> 00:07:20,106
Most of all…

85
00:07:22,775 --> 00:07:27,613
I'll miss having someone I knew
would always be there for me,

86
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:29,574
no matter what happens in life.

87
00:07:40,334 --> 00:07:43,004
Thank you for your love, Mario.

88
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:47,508
<i>For loving us more</i>
<i>than we could ever ask for.</i>

89
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:54,724
<i>For a love so pure</i>
<i>that it reaches all the way to heaven.</i>

90
00:07:57,643 --> 00:08:00,897
<i>A love that never asked</i>
<i>for anything in return.</i>

91
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:04,400
<i>A love that never complained.</i>

92
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:07,695
A love that is unconditional.

93
00:08:11,699 --> 00:08:14,327
Don't worry, my love.

94
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:16,829
I'll take care of the children.

95
00:08:24,795 --> 00:08:26,589
Rest now, my love.

96
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:31,260
We'll see each other again.
Just wait for me.

97
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:33,262
Oh, Mom.

98
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:38,100
To Dad Mario.

99
00:08:39,602 --> 00:08:41,979
To the father of all of you.

100
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:45,900
To the man I love.

101
00:09:10,299 --> 00:09:11,926
Always leaving us behind.

102
00:09:14,428 --> 00:09:16,264
Always leaving.

103
00:09:31,529 --> 00:09:33,906
NORBERTO S. RUIZ
GENERAL

104
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:36,492
Say hi to our friends for me up there.

105
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:44,792
Our buddy is happy up there now.

106
00:10:49,106 --> 00:10:50,858
You should've seen it.

107
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:55,988
Everyone here had so much
to say about you, Dad.

108
00:10:56,781 --> 00:10:58,240
Everyone from around here.

109
00:11:00,076 --> 00:11:01,118
It was all good.

110
00:11:02,203 --> 00:11:03,704
There weren't any haters.

111
00:11:25,601 --> 00:11:27,186
I'll miss you, Dad.

112
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:25,494
This is my promise to you, Dad.

113
00:12:29,582 --> 00:12:32,126
I'll make everyone
who did this to you pay.

114
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:29,558
Child.

115
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:30,601
Mama, Papa.

116
00:13:32,978 --> 00:13:33,854
Chiara.

117
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:39,568
Yes, what happened, child?

118
00:13:40,444 --> 00:13:41,362
What happened was,

119
00:13:41,445 --> 00:13:43,697
just the other day, we were locked up.

120
00:13:43,781 --> 00:13:47,034
Then suddenly, they put us
on our private plane,

121
00:13:47,117 --> 00:13:49,995
and now we're here, in Prague.

122
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:59,380
We thought it was the end for both of us.

123
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:13,644
But why are we here, child?

124
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:21,110
Viktor and Donabel escaped!

125
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:26,866
How did that happen?

126
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:29,451
They were our last hope

127
00:14:29,535 --> 00:14:31,829
to pin out Chiara.

128
00:14:31,912 --> 00:14:35,040
And they still managed to escape!

129
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:50,931
Sir,

130
00:14:52,057 --> 00:14:53,934
that's not even the bad news yet.

131
00:14:59,064 --> 00:15:01,400
We have reason to believe

132
00:15:01,483 --> 00:15:04,612
that they've already left the country.

133
00:15:06,822 --> 00:15:07,823
What?

134
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:18,959
Why, my dear?

135
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:31,805
She's the new leader of the Concordat.

136
00:15:32,431 --> 00:15:33,974
What are you doing here?

137
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,985
Just because you married an foreigner,

138
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:46,862
you think you're better than everyone?

139
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:55,663
I don't care about
your plans for your life.

140
00:15:56,538 --> 00:15:57,831
Don't get near my daughter

141
00:15:57,915 --> 00:15:59,541
and try to wash her brain.

142
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:00,793
Wash her brain?

143
00:16:00,876 --> 00:16:03,921
Brainwash, duh. You slowpoke.

144
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:08,801
Mama, no one's being brainwashed here.

145
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:12,262
This is my own decision.

146
00:16:13,055 --> 00:16:17,059
And Mama Yaya will be part
of my plans moving forward.

147
00:16:21,689 --> 00:16:25,442
The Concordat always manages
to slip through our fingers.

148
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:28,570
Is this agency even useful anymore?

149
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:31,407
Maybe you've forgotten?

150
00:16:32,199 --> 00:16:34,034
She killed

151
00:16:34,827 --> 00:16:36,620
Mario Pinagpala,

152
00:16:37,121 --> 00:16:39,039
who was Mikoy's father!

153
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:47,715
You're making the wrong decision.

154
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:49,675
Didn't you say

155
00:16:49,758 --> 00:16:51,510
you wanted a quiet life,

156
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:54,346
and that you loved Mikoy so much?

157
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:56,807
Didn't you two
already plan a life together?

158
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:57,975
What happened?

159
00:16:58,058 --> 00:16:59,768
Stop pretending.

160
00:17:00,519 --> 00:17:02,021
Let's face it.

161
00:17:02,104 --> 00:17:06,900
We all know there's really no future
for Mikoy and me.

162
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:12,031
I can't escape who I really am.

163
00:17:49,651 --> 00:17:52,112
NORBERTO S. RUIZ
GENERAL

164
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:18,180
And you were the one who killed him?

165
00:18:22,226 --> 00:18:23,977
He wasn't supposed to be there.

166
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:26,313
He shouldn't have gotten involved.

167
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:27,981
He shouldn't have
gotten caught up in this.

168
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:29,233
How could you do that, child?

169
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:31,151
What did Mikoy say?

170
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:33,821
How did you explain what happened to him?

171
00:18:33,904 --> 00:18:35,697
Well, I don't need to explain anymore

172
00:18:35,781 --> 00:18:37,991
because we don't need
to see each other anymore.

173
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,957
that if we keep forcing this relationship,

174
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:46,583
more people will get caught
in the crossfire.

175
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:48,502
More family members

176
00:18:48,585 --> 00:18:51,797
or innocent lives could be lost.

177
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,178
Mikoy and I are over.

178
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:04,643
The illusion that I could still
have a happy and normal life is over.

179
00:19:09,439 --> 00:19:12,985
Our assumption is that Chiara
is no longer in the country.

180
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:26,874
So there's nothing we can do?

181
00:19:33,714 --> 00:19:34,840
Where is she now?

182
00:19:40,512 --> 00:19:43,140
She has a lot of allies there,
so she's safe.

183
00:19:43,223 --> 00:19:47,019
That's also where Viktor and Donabel
got their private jet.

184
00:19:59,698 --> 00:20:02,492
I have to accept the fact
that I'm a Valtrovi,

185
00:20:02,576 --> 00:20:03,994
that this is my life,

186
00:20:04,786 --> 00:20:08,248
and that I'll die as a true mafia.

187
00:20:14,838 --> 00:20:17,925
And if he ever threatens my position,

188
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:20,677
or derails any of my plans,

189
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:24,765
I'll send him to where his father is now.

190
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:35,817
Don't we have connections in Prague?

191
00:20:35,901 --> 00:20:37,236
With the Czech authorities?

192
00:20:38,278 --> 00:20:40,489
Well, yes, but…

193
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:43,492
when it comes to sharing information,

194
00:20:43,575 --> 00:20:47,371
or getting their cooperation
to apprehend Chiara,

195
00:20:47,454 --> 00:20:49,581
I doubt it very much.

196
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:58,507
And with their influence,

197
00:20:59,299 --> 00:21:03,720
I doubt there's much
we can do to hold them accountable.

198
00:21:03,804 --> 00:21:05,347
So that's it?

199
00:21:05,430 --> 00:21:06,723
We're not going to do anything?

200
00:21:12,229 --> 00:21:14,481
It doesn't matter whether
you can do something or not.

201
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:16,817
I made a promise

202
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:19,444
that I'll make everyone
who did this to Dad pay,

203
00:21:20,612 --> 00:21:21,863
and that's what I'll do.

204
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:24,491
All I ask, Sir Norberto,

205
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:27,077
is please stay out of my way.

206
00:21:41,842 --> 00:21:46,263
Looks like Donabel
and Viktor don't like me.

207
00:21:51,101 --> 00:21:53,603
Don't mind them.
I'm sure they'll come around.

208
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:58,400
If you hadn't decided
to become the Concordat,

209
00:21:58,483 --> 00:22:00,569
they'd still be in prison right now.

210
00:22:02,696 --> 00:22:04,531
By the way, where's Rahmboy?

211
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:08,035
He stayed behind in the Philippines,

212
00:22:09,328 --> 00:22:12,539
to do some mop-up operations.

213
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:18,420
And to make sure everything is clean.

214
00:22:22,674 --> 00:22:25,761
Norberto's agency won't bother us anymore.

215
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:29,181
They have no reason
to investigate us anymore.

216
00:22:34,811 --> 00:22:37,314
I don't think Mikoy will be a problem.

217
00:22:44,112 --> 00:22:48,158
Maybe he can convince these people

218
00:22:48,241 --> 00:22:52,496
and turn everyone against us.

219
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:58,752
Mikoy.

220
00:23:00,587 --> 00:23:01,546
Mikoy.

221
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:05,842
Mikoy, where are you going?

222
00:23:08,386 --> 00:23:09,513
If I'm not mistaken,

223
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:12,516
I am no longer
a police asset of this agency.

224
00:23:16,186 --> 00:23:18,146
You don't get to run my life anymore.

225
00:23:21,108 --> 00:23:22,901
I understand what you're feeling.

226
00:23:25,737 --> 00:23:26,613
Really?

227
00:23:29,574 --> 00:23:30,951
You have no idea

228
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:33,411
what I'm going through.

229
00:23:45,549 --> 00:23:49,177
Our top priority is how
to control the Concordat.

230
00:23:51,304 --> 00:23:53,014
What about you? What will you do?

231
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:55,183
I will go back to the Philippines.

232
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:58,311
To make sure that Rahmboy
cleared all the mess.

233
00:23:58,395 --> 00:24:01,148
There’s still someone who’s in my way
in leading the Concordat.

234
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:02,149
Who?

235
00:24:04,151 --> 00:24:07,362
If you’re going to kill me, Chiara,
or anyone else,

236
00:24:07,445 --> 00:24:10,574
the hurt that you are feeling now
won’t go away.

237
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:17,706
The day that you killed my father.

238
00:24:26,506 --> 00:24:27,591
What do you want?

239
00:24:30,468 --> 00:24:34,514
We are the agency that can bend rules
for the sake of justice.
